  "question": "What does the Ge'ez text of the Ezana Stone say?",
  "answer": "The available source on the Ezana Stone does not specify which of the inscription's three language versions the quoted text comes from, so it cannot be confirmed that the passage given is specifically the Ge'ez text rather than one of the other versions of the trilingual monument [S5]. That source is presented in English, with the text reading: \"Aeizanas, king of the Aksumites, Himyarites and Raeidan, the Ethiopians, the Sabaeans and Silei, Tiamo and the Beja and Kasu, king of kings, son of the invincible god Ares\" [S5]. No transliteration or original-script rendering of the Ge'ez wording is provided in this source, only this English-language text [S5].",
